meta {
  name: Remember when
  type: http
  seq: 36
}

get {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/remember?q=the walk by the river
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  q: the walk by the river
  ~limit: 10
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  "Remember when" (FR-204, ADR-0054): a question in plain words, answered with the days of your archive most relevant to it, most relevant first, each day whole. Never generated text: every answer is an entry one of you wrote. No cursor: limit is 1 to 20, 10 when left out, and fewer days, or none, is usual.

  Two rankings are fused: by the question's words, and by its meaning while the bond's semantic search is on and a provider is configured. With neither (production names no provider yet), it is the words' ranking alone, which needs every word of q in one entry: "the walk by the river" finds a day only if one entry holds all five words; "river" alone is kinder. Your partner's entry is found only once it has been revealed.

  q follows search's rules: blank, or longer than 100 characters, is 422 on q, never sent back. Thirty questions an hour.
}
